"""
Liquid in a tank as a `VariableMass` on the hull, fed by the tank's volume
and level (from an `IncompressibleFlowComponents` `OpenTank_2Port`): the mass
is `rho · volume` and its centre sits at half the liquid height above the
tank bottom `r_tank` in the ship frame.
"""
component TankLiquidMass
  "Hull frame"
  frame_a = Frame3D()
  "Liquid volume [m³]"
  volume = RealInput()
  "Liquid level above the tank bottom [m]"
  level = RealInput()
  "Liquid mass [kg]"
  mass = RealOutput()
  "Tank bottom centre in the ship frame [x fwd, y port, z up]"
  parameter r_tank::Length[3] = [50, 8, 1]
  "Liquid density [kg/m³]"
  parameter rho::Density = 1025
  mount = MultibodyComponents.FixedTranslation(r = r_tank, render = false)
  liquid = VariableMass()
relations
  connect(frame_a, mount.frame_a)
  connect(mount.frame_b, liquid.frame_a)
  mass = rho * volume
  liquid.m = mass
  liquid.z_cm = 0.5 * level
end

"""
Centrifugal pump as a pressure-flow relation with a check valve.

Affinity-law characteristic `H = s² H0 - k Q|Q| - k_lin Q` for the head
rise from `port_a` to `port_b`, with `s = speed` the speed fraction, so the
delivered flow follows from the pressures of the network (a resistive
element, not a flow source). The small laminar term `k_lin Q` keeps the
flow-pressure relation non-singular at zero flow, which the initialization
needs. At `s = 0` the pump is a quadratic resistance, and reverse flow
meets the much larger `k_back` (a smooth check valve), so a stopped branch
passes no water. Isenthalpic transport; the hydraulic power is `rho g H Q`.
"""
component CentrifugalPump
  extends IncompressibleFlowComponents.Interfaces.PartialTwoPortTransport
  "Speed fraction N / N_nominal, 0 = stopped"
  speed = RealInput()
  "Hydraulic power delivered to the fluid [W]"
  power = RealOutput()
  "Shut-off head at nominal speed [m]"
  parameter H0::Length = 15
  "Head-flow coefficient: H = s² H0 - k Q|Q| [s²/m⁵]"
  parameter k::Real = 3600
  "Resistance coefficient for reverse flow (check valve)"
  parameter k_back::Real = 100 * 3600
  "Laminar head-loss coefficient [s/m²]"
  parameter k_lin::Real = 10
  "Flow scale of the smooth forward/reverse transition [m³/s]"
  parameter Q_eps::Real = 1e-4
  "Temperature at which the medium density is evaluated"
  parameter T_ref::Temperature = 288.15
  parameter g::Acceleration = 9.80665
  variable rho::Density
  "Volume flow from port_a to port_b"
  variable Q::VolumeFlowRate
  "Head rise from port_a to port_b"
  variable head::Length
  variable k_eff::Real
relations
  rho = IncompressibleFlowComponents.Media.density(port_a.medium, T_ref)
  Q = m_flow / rho
  k_eff = k + (k_back - k) * (0.5 - 0.5 * tanh(Q / Q_eps))
  head = speed^2 * H0 - k_eff * Q * abs(Q) - k_lin * Q
  dp = -rho * g * head
  power = rho * g * head * Q
end

"""
Anti-heeling tanks and transfer pumps as an `IncompressibleFlowComponents`
circuit, to be extended by a ship assembly (fluid ports must not pass through
wrapper components: the stream expansion then leaves the port enthalpies as
runaway states, so this is a partial that the ship test extends).

Two `OpenTank_2Port` tanks (`tank_a` at `r_tank_a`, `tank_b` at `r_tank_b`;
each liquid also a `TankLiquidMass` on the `hull` frame) are joined by two
antiparallel branches, a `CentrifugalPump` and a `ValveLinear` in series for
A→B and the same for B→A. The extender sets `flow_cmd` [m³/h] and
`direction` (+1 = A→B, -1 = B→A): the active pump's speed fraction is
`flow_cmd / Q_nominal` through a `T_pump` spin-up ramp, its valve opens
through a `T_valve` actuator ramp once more than 1 m³/h is requested, and
closes again as the receiving tank nears `fill_max` or the emptying one
nears `fill_min`. The idle branch has its pump stopped (a resistance with a
check valve) and its valve shut. The water actually moved follows the pump
characteristic against the tank level difference and the valve losses.

The ramps also keep the fluid loop free of jumps: `direction` and `flow_cmd`
come from a clocked controller, and every clock tick re-checks the
algebraic residual without re-solving it, so a discrete command must reach
the pump and valve equations only through a continuous state.
"""
partial component AntiHeelingCircuit
  "Hull frame the tank liquids act on"
  hull = Frame3D()
  path medium::IncompressibleFlowComponents.Media.AbstractMedium = IncompressibleFlowComponents.Media.ConstantIncompressible(density = 1025.0)
  "Tank A bottom centre in the ship frame"
  parameter r_tank_a::Length[3] = [50, 8, 1]
  "Tank B bottom centre in the ship frame"
  parameter r_tank_b::Length[3] = [50, -8, 1]
  "Tank volume [m³]"
  parameter V_tank::Real = 100
  "Tank height [m]"
  parameter H_tank::Length = 5
  "Initial fill fraction of both tanks"
  parameter fill_start::Real = 0.45
  parameter rho_liquid::Density = 1025
  parameter T_liquid::Temperature = 288.15
  "Pump nominal capacity [m³/h] at full speed"
  parameter Q_nominal::Real = 200
  "Pump shut-off head at full speed [m]"
  parameter H0::Length = 15
  "Pump head-flow coefficient [s²/m⁵]"
  parameter k_pump::Real = 3600
  "Valve sizing point: mass flow through the fully open valve"
  parameter m_flow_nominal::MassFlowRate = 57
  "Valve sizing point: pressure drop at m_flow_nominal"
  parameter dp_nominal::Pressure = 3e4
  "Highest fill fraction of the receiving tank"
  parameter fill_max::Real = 0.85
  "Lowest fill fraction of the emptying tank"
  parameter fill_min::Real = 0.05
  "Width of the fill-limit ramp"
  parameter fill_band::Real = 0.02
  "Valve actuators: openings ramp at 1/T_valve per second"
  parameter T_valve::Time = 5
  "Pump speed ramp: rest to full speed in T_pump seconds"
  parameter T_pump::Time = 5
  tank_a = IncompressibleFlowComponents.Volumes.OpenTank_2Port(height = H_tank, A_cross = V_tank / H_tank, p_ambient = 101325, T_start = T_liquid, level_start = fill_start * H_tank)
  tank_b = IncompressibleFlowComponents.Volumes.OpenTank_2Port(height = H_tank, A_cross = V_tank / H_tank, p_ambient = 101325, T_start = T_liquid, level_start = fill_start * H_tank)
  mass_a = TankLiquidMass(r_tank = r_tank_a, rho = rho_liquid)
  mass_b = TankLiquidMass(r_tank = r_tank_b, rho = rho_liquid)
  pump_ab = CentrifugalPump(H0 = H0, k = k_pump, k_back = 100 * k_pump, T_ref = T_liquid)
  pump_ba = CentrifugalPump(H0 = H0, k = k_pump, k_back = 100 * k_pump, T_ref = T_liquid)
  valve_ab = IncompressibleFlowComponents.Valves.ValveLinear(opening_mode = IncompressibleFlowComponents.BoundarySourceMode.InputConnector(), m_flow_nominal = m_flow_nominal, dp_nominal = dp_nominal)
  valve_ba = IncompressibleFlowComponents.Valves.ValveLinear(opening_mode = IncompressibleFlowComponents.BoundarySourceMode.InputConnector(), m_flow_nominal = m_flow_nominal, dp_nominal = dp_nominal)
  act_ab = BlockComponents.Nonlinear.SlewRateLimiter(rising = 1 / T_valve, td = 0.05)
  act_ba = BlockComponents.Nonlinear.SlewRateLimiter(rising = 1 / T_valve, td = 0.05)
  spd_ab = BlockComponents.Nonlinear.SlewRateLimiter(rising = 1 / T_pump, td = 0.05)
  spd_ba = BlockComponents.Nonlinear.SlewRateLimiter(rising = 1 / T_pump, td = 0.05)
  "Requested transfer rate [m³/h], set by the extender"
  variable flow_cmd::Real
  "+1 transfers A→B, -1 transfers B→A, set by the extender"
  variable direction::Real
  "Mass flow A→B through the branches [kg/s]"
  variable m_flow_ab::Real
  variable on_ab::Real
  variable on_ba::Real
  variable speed_frac::Real
  variable fill_a::Real
  variable fill_b::Real
relations
  continuity(medium, tank_a.port1.medium)
  connect(tank_a.port1, pump_ab.port_a, valve_ba.port_b)
  connect(tank_b.port1, pump_ba.port_a, valve_ab.port_b)
  connect(pump_ab.port_b, valve_ab.port_a)
  connect(pump_ba.port_b, valve_ba.port_a)
  connect(hull, mass_a.frame_a, mass_b.frame_a)
  mass_a.volume = tank_a.fluidVolume
  mass_a.level = tank_a.level
  mass_b.volume = tank_b.fluidVolume
  mass_b.level = tank_b.level
  fill_a = tank_a.levelNormalized
  fill_b = tank_b.levelNormalized
  on_ab = ifelse(direction > 0.5, 1, 0)
  on_ba = ifelse(direction < -0.5, 1, 0)
  speed_frac = clamp(flow_cmd / Q_nominal, 0, 1)
  spd_ab.u = on_ab * speed_frac
  spd_ba.u = on_ba * speed_frac
  pump_ab.speed = spd_ab.y
  pump_ba.speed = spd_ba.y
  act_ab.u = on_ab * clamp(flow_cmd, 0, 1) * clamp((fill_max - fill_b) / fill_band, 0, 1) * clamp((fill_a - fill_min) / fill_band, 0, 1)
  act_ba.u = on_ba * clamp(flow_cmd, 0, 1) * clamp((fill_max - fill_a) / fill_band, 0, 1) * clamp((fill_b - fill_min) / fill_band, 0, 1)
  valve_ab.opening = act_ab.y
  valve_ba.opening = act_ba.y
  m_flow_ab = pump_ab.m_flow - pump_ba.m_flow
end
